7. Processing pipeline and workers

Build a reusable processing pipeline:

Select a local file.
 Validate size and type.
 Detect the format.
 Read the file.
 Parse it with an appropriate local library.
 Normalize data into shared internal types.
 Execute the requested operation.
 Generate a preview.
 Validate the output.
 Export a Blob.
 Download the result.
 Clean up temporary resources.

Use workers for CPU-intensive operations where beneficial.

Implement worker communication with typed request and response messages.

Support progress, errors, cancellation, and cleanup where the underlying task supports them.

Never invent progress or report success before processing finishes.

Avoid loading the same file repeatedly.

Use virtualization for large tables and configurable resource limits for expensive operations.

Never silently truncate data.

